{"challenge_uid":"4bb69e94-46d9-4d3f-a2a1-6e6a917fed56","challenge_id":6,"challenge_name":"Decryption","unit":41,"difficulty_levels":["easy","moderate","hard"],"total_steps":7,"steps":[{"difficulty":"easy","step_id":1,"description":"<p><span style=\"font-family: Arial; font-size: 15px; white-space: pre-wrap; text-decoration-skip-ink: none;\">In encryption, a string is converted to a non-readable form. Decryption is the opposite process whereby the encrypted string is reverted to the original form. Hence, the algorithm to perform decryption is the reverse of that for encryption. For example, if you add 1 to the code of a character in encryption, then you'll have to minus 1 for decryption. Also, if you have multiple steps in encryption, then you'll have to do the steps in reverse order for decryption. </span></p><p><span style=\"font-family: Arial; font-size: 15px; white-space: pre-wrap; text-decoration-skip-ink: none;\">A simple </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial; font-size: 15px; white-space: pre-wrap; font-weight: bold; text-decoration-skip-ink: none;\">encryption </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial; font-size: 15px; white-space: pre-wrap; text-decoration-skip-ink: none;\">of a string is as follow:\nThe character code of each character is increased by 2 (i.e. convert each character to its code, add 2 and then convert back to a character with the new code). \nFor example, \"ABC\" will become \"CDE\" after encryption.\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-family: Arial; font-size: 15px; white-space: pre-wrap; text-decoration-skip-ink: none;\">Write a </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial; font-size: 15px; white-space: pre-wrap; font-weight: bold; text-decoration-skip-ink: none;\">function </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial; font-size: 15px; white-space: pre-wrap; text-decoration-skip-ink: none;\">that takes in an encrypted string to perform </span><span style=\"font-family: Arial; font-size: 15px; white-space: pre-wrap; font-weight: bold; text-decoration-skip-ink: none;\">decryption</span><span style=\"font-family: Arial; font-size: 15px; white-space: pre-wrap; text-decoration-skip-ink: none;\">. It will then return the decrypted string.\n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-family: Arial; font-size: 15px; white-space: pre-wrap; text-decoration-skip-ink: none;\">Write a program that asks the user to input an encrypted string. It will then call your function to decrypt it and display the returned result. \n</span></p><p><span style=\"font-family: Arial; font-size: 15px; white-space: pre-wrap; text-decoration-skip-ink: none;\">Follow the test output display format and comment your codes.</span><br></p><p><span style=\"font-family: Arial; font-size: 15px; white-space: pre-wrap; text-decoration-skip-ink: none;\"><u segoe=\"\" ui\",=\"\" roboto,=\"\" \"helvetica=\"\" neue\",=\"\" arial,=\"\" \"noto=\"\" sans\",=\"\" sans-serif,=\"\" \"apple=\"\" color=\"\" emoji\",=\"\" \"segoe=\"\" ui=\"\" symbol\",=\"\" emoji\";=\"\" font-size:=\"\" 16px;=\"\" white-space:=\"\" normal;\"=\"\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Test Input</span><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">\n</span></u></span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 0, 0); font-family: Arial; font-size: 15px; white-space: pre-wrap;\">CDEFG\n</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 0, 0); font-family: Arial; font-size: 15px; white-space: pre-wrap;\">jcemgt</span></p><div><u segoe=\"\" ui\",=\"\" roboto,=\"\" \"helvetica=\"\" neue\",=\"\" arial,=\"\" \"noto=\"\" sans\",=\"\" sans-serif,=\"\" \"apple=\"\" color=\"\" emoji\",=\"\" \"segoe=\"\" ui=\"\" symbol\",=\"\" emoji\";=\"\" font-size:=\"\" 16px;=\"\" white-space:=\"\" normal;\"=\"\" style=\"font-family: Arial; font-size: 15px; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">Test Output (</span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 0, 0); font-weight: bold;\">Red Text - User Input</span></u><span segoe=\"\" ui\",=\"\" roboto,=\"\" \"helvetica=\"\" neue\",=\"\" arial,=\"\" \"noto=\"\" sans\",=\"\" sans-serif,=\"\" \"app